# Scoreboard-local ignores.
#
# Repo-wide rules live in the root .gitignore and already cover .DS_Store,
# .venv/, __pycache__/, *.pyc and .env. Do not repeat them here; this file is
# only for what is specific to the Scoreboard.
#
# The data product IS committed. outputs/scoreboard.db and the three CSV
# exports beside it are what someone clones this directory for, so nothing
# below may exclude them.

# SQLite writes these beside the database while a transaction is open and
# removes them on commit. They are never part of the data, and a stray one left
# behind by a crashed run must not be committed.
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# The README tells you to copy the database before experimenting, because most
# commands open it read-write. Those copies stay local. The canonical database
# is the one exception.
*.db
!outputs/scoreboard.db

# Run transcripts from collect/. A routine run is noise -- large, append-only,
# and it changes every time, so committing them all would bury the diffs that
# matter. The transcript of a run that produced PUBLISHED data is a different
# thing: it is the provenance record for that corpus, and it gets allowlisted
# here by name, the same way the canonical database is above.
logs/*.log

# Working files from collect/. Each run writes the lead or row it is about to
# ingest as JSON, then calls source-add / screen-add on it. Once the command
# returns, the database holds the content and the file is just the envelope it
# arrived in. The README is tracked so the directory exists in a fresh clone.
scratch/*
!scratch/README.md
